<div id="2026-10-05-3d-library-thumbnails-nfs-merge" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-10-05 — 3D library thumbnails moved to NFS; main merge completed on InventoryAccounting</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> Large generated PNG and SVG thumbnail files (previously committed into <code>root/static/images/3d/library/</code> by an earlier AI change, causing git bloat and merge blocks) were removed from git tracking and the working tree. The small, correct raster PNG versions (~25 MB total for 1,373 files) were migrated to the NFS volume at <code>/data/nfs/3d/thumbnails/library/</code> using direct file operations aligned with the File manager / NfsPath patterns. The sole unmerged conflict in <code>Comserv/lib/Comserv/Model/AI2/Router.pm</code> was resolved by retaining the modern queue-based failover/health/chain logic. The merge from main was completed with a clean commit. Thumbnails for browse and model detail pages remain referenced via <code>printing_3d_models.thumbnail_url</code> (with .svg→.png substitution in templates).</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why.</strong> Static directories under git are unsuitable for generated or large binary assets. The 3D system already uses NFS for STLs and other files via <code>Comserv::Util::NfsPath</code>, <code>File</code> model <code>upload_and_record</code>, and <code>/data/nfs</code>. Storing SVGs (full STL triangle meshes) or even converted PNGs in git bloats the repo, breaks merges across worktrees/branches, and violates the "file manager for assets" convention. The prior "fix" on main had lost the files; copies were available locally for proper migration.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>Comserv/lib/Comserv/Model/AI2/Router.pm</code> (conflict resolution), <code>Comserv/root/static/images/3d/library/</code> (removed from index + tree), <code>/data/nfs/3d/thumbnails/library/</code> (target), <code>.gitignore</code> (already protected the path), <code>Comserv/root/3d/browse.tt</code> and <code>model_detail.tt</code> (no functional change), merge commit b357e19fe. Documentation updates in <code>Comserv/root/Documentation/features/3d_printing.tt</code> and this changelog entry.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Time spent.</strong> Approximately 2–3 hours (context gathering across git status, code searches for thumbnail/NfsPath/File handling, asset inspection and NFS copy, targeted patch for conflict resolution in the complex failover method, verification of index/working tree/merge state, documentation updates, and final merge commit with message).</p>
</div>